<article class="env-construction" id="02BZ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02BZ">Construction <span data-tag="02BZ">4.5.1.23</span> <span class="named">(The Homotopy Bicategory of $\infty $-Categories)</span>.</a> We define a strict bicategory $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}$ as follows: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The objects of $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}$ are $\infty $-categories. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ are $\infty $-categories, then $\underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}} }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) = \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}},\operatorname{\mathcal{D}})}$ is the homotopy category of the functor $\infty $-category $\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, and $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ are $\infty $-categories, then the composition law on $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}$ is given by 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \begin{eqnarray*}  \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \times \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) &amp;  = &amp;  (\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{D}},\operatorname{\mathcal{E}})}) \times (\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})}) \\ &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{(\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{D}},\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \times \operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}},\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}))} \\ &amp;  \xrightarrow {\circ } &amp;  \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})} \\ &amp;  = &amp;  \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}). \end{eqnarray*}
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> We will refer to $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}$ as the <em>homotopy bicategory of $\infty $-categories</em>. We let $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$ denote the pith of $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}$, in the sense of Construction <a data-tag="00AL" href="/tag/00AL">2.2.8.9</a>; we will refer to $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$ as the <em>homotopy $(2,1)$-category of $\infty $-categories</em>. </p>
</article>
